<title>POLAND: BYTOM TO CUT 288 JOBS NEXT MONTH.</title>
<headline>BYTOM TO CUT 288 JOBS NEXT MONTH.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish garment maker Bytom SA will lay off 288 workers in February to cut production and shut down one of its six plants, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company will also not hire workers returning from maternity leaves in 1997, it added.</p>
<p>&quot;The dismissals...are connected to a necessity to adjust the plants' production potential with the actual sales possibilities,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>The dismissals will take effect on February 28.</p>
<p>Company officials were not immediately available for comment. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
